{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Cutting {\n\n    private static int[] convertStringToIntArray(String input) {\n        return Arrays.stream(input.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\"))\n                     .mapToInt(Integer::parseInt)\n                     .toArray();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean isEvenOddBalanced(int[] array, int boundary) {\n        int evens = 0, odds = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= boundary; i++) {\n            if (array[i] % 2 == 0) evens++;\n            else odds++;\n        }\n        return evens == odds;\n    }\n\n    private static int locateCheapestValidCut(int[] values, int coinsLeft, Set<Integer> blocked) {\n        int bestPos = -1;\n        int minExpense = coinsLeft + 1;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < values.length - 1; i++) {\n            int expense = Math.abs(values[i] - values[i + 1]);\n            if (expense < minExpense && isEvenOddBalanced(values, i) && !blocked.contains(i)) {\n                minExpense = expense;\n                bestPos = i;\n            }\n        }\n        return bestPos;\n    }\n\n    public int calculateMaxCuts(int totalItems, int initialCoins, int[] coinValues) {\n        int coins = initialCoins;\n        int cuts = 0;\n        Set<Integer> usedPositions = new HashSet<>();\n\n        while (coins > 0) {\n            int pos = locateCheapestValidCut(coinValues, coins, usedPositions);\n            if (pos == -1) break;\n\n            usedPositions.add(pos);\n            coins -= Math.abs(coinValues[pos] - coinValues[pos + 1]);\n            cuts++;\n        }\n        return cuts;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out))) {\n\n            int[] first = convertStringToIntArray(br.readLine());\n            int[] second = convertStringToIntArray(br.readLine());\n\n            Cutting instance = new Cutting();\n            int answer = instance.calculateMaxCuts(first[0], first[1], second);\n\n            bw.write(Integer.toString(answer));\n            bw.newLine();\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef convert_string_to_int_array(input_str):\n    return list(map(int, input_str.strip().split()))\n\ndef is_even_odd_balanced(array, boundary):\n    evens = 0\n    odds = 0\n    for i in range(boundary + 1):\n        if array[i] % 2 == 0:\n            evens += 1\n        else:\n            odds += 1\n    return evens == odds\n\ndef locate_cheapest_valid_cut(values, coins_left, blocked):\n    best_pos = -1\n    min_expense = coins_left + 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(values) - 1):\n        expense = abs(values[i] - values[i + 1])\n        if expense < min_expense and is_even_odd_balanced(values, i) and i not in blocked:\n            min_expense = expense\n            best_pos = i\n    return best_pos\n\ndef 